RC - background services

Services are scripts in /etc/rc.d/NAME.lua that define start() and
optionally stop(), status() or other commands. Services listed in
/etc/rc.cfg start at boot.

  rc                    list services
  rc NAME start         start (also stop, restart, status)
  rc NAME enable        start at boot (disable to undo)

A service usually registers event listeners or starts a detached
thread in start(). Settings for it go in /etc/rc.cfg as
NAME = {...}; the script sees them as `args`. See
/etc/rc.d/example.lua and /etc/rc.d/beacon.lua.
